  "explanation": "Since $f(x)=ax^3+bx$, we have $f(2)=8a+2b=16$ and $f(3)=27a+3b=54$. Simplifying the first equation by dividing by 2 gives $4a+b=8$. Simplifying the second by dividing by 3 gives $9a+b=18$. Subtracting the first from the second: $(9a+b)-(4a+b)=18-8$, which gives $5a=10$, so $a=2$.\n\nWhy A is incorrect:\n\nThis results from using only one condition and making an incorrect assumption about the value of $b$, then solving incompletely.",
